    "article": "Lena planned a day trip for two guests who had never visited Harbor City. She chose a museum where visitors can learn about local ships and a market that sells food from the region. The train that leaves at 8:10 arrives before the museum opens, so the guests will have enough time for breakfast. Lena bought the train tickets in advance and sent the boarding information to the guests. She also marked the station where they need to transfer. In the afternoon, they can take a boat tour, which is included in the city pass. If the weather is poor, they will visit an indoor exhibition instead. The friend who suggested the boat tour said it was worth doing because it shows a different side of the city. Lena's plan does not fill every minute. She wants the guests to make the most of the day without feeling rushed.",
