    "article": "Both friendly relationships and clear boundaries can improve a workplace. At River Design, new employees are invited to a monthly lunch, but attendance is optional. The event helps people get on well and makes it easier to ask coworkers for help. It is not only a social activity but also a chance to meet people from other departments.\n\nHowever, employees do not have to share personal information. Either joining the lunch or taking a quiet break is acceptable. The company asks managers to avoid discussing private performance issues at social events because work and personal time should sometimes be kept separate. If two colleagues fall out with each other, they are still expected to communicate politely about their tasks. Neither friendship nor disagreement changes the rules for completing work. The policy is designed to support choice: people may build friendships, but they should not feel pressure to do so. In practice, a comfortable workplace depends on both respect and cooperation.",
