    "goal": "that + 完整子句：The report says that the time is wrong.；what + 不完整子句：Check what the report says.；間接問句用陳述語序：Do you know whether it is posted?",
    "article": "A travel company used to post customer photographs on social media after receiving permission. Recently, staff noticed that some popular destination pictures were generated by AI. They looked realistic, but the beaches and hotel rooms did not actually exist. This made it hard for customers to know what had been created by people and what had been produced by a system.\n\nThe company did not ban AI images. Instead, it introduced a clear label and required a manual review before any advertising image was posted. The new policy states that staff must identify the source, check whether the picture represents a real service, and store the approval record. An inaccurate image can turn customers away because it may shatter the illusion that all online content is reliable.\n\nAfter one month, the marketing team reported that fewer people clicked the AI-labelled posts, but complaints also fell. The manager said that the purpose of the policy was not to make every image traditional. It was to give customers enough information to judge the content. What matters is whether the source and purpose are made clear, not whether a computer tool was used at all.",
    "listening": "Maya: The event page automatically created a summary, but it says the workshop starts at two. The approved schedule says three.\nBen: Then the summary is inaccurate. Do you know whether anyone has posted it?\nMaya: Not yet. The system saved it as a draft.\nBen: Good. Please correct the time and contact the speaker to confirm the room. I'll ask for a manual review before we publish it.\nMaya: I'll do that now and attach the approved schedule so the reviewer can compare both versions.",
    "grammarNote": "• that + 完整子句：The report says that the time is wrong.；what + 不完整子句：Check what the report says.；間接問句用陳述語序：Do you know whether it is posted?\n• 常錯：Do you know where is the room?。辨認：Please tell us ___ the system needs. A that B what。無提示：Do you know when the event ___? 遷移：用 whether/what/that 各寫一個查核問題。",
