    "title": "追蹤新聞但保留休息",
    "stage": "TOEIC 應用",
    "grammar": "G18＋資訊功能辨認",
    "goal": "先判斷問題功能：purpose、what changed、what stayed、why、next。原句 instead of 常把舊資訊放成干擾。",
    "article": "Kai follows transport news because he commutes across the city every weekday. First thing in the morning, he checks whether any train delays have happened overnight. He also receives notifications from the transit company throughout the day. These updates can be useful: last Tuesday, one message told him that his usual platform was closed, so he chose another route before leaving work.\n\nHowever, Kai used to receive too many alerts. Some repeated the same information, while others concerned lines he never used. The constant messages made it difficult to focus. He therefore changed the settings so that only major delays on two routes would appear. He has already noticed a difference. The information he receives is more relevant, and he no longer checks his phone every few minutes.\n\nKai still follows the news, but he now takes a break from it when no action is required. This does not mean ignoring important information. It means separating an update that changes his next step from one that is merely interesting. If a notice says service will stop, he acts. If it only reviews an event that has ended, he reads it later.\n\nAt the end of each week, Kai checks whether his settings still match his travel pattern. When he began an evening course on another line, he added that route but kept minor promotional notices switched off. His goal is not to receive less information at any cost; it is to receive useful information at the right time.",
    "listening": "Good afternoon, passengers. This message is to inform you that the 5:40 service to West Bay will depart from Platform 7 instead of Platform 5. The departure time has not changed. Passengers who have already reached Platform 5 should proceed to Platform 7 by using the footbridge. Please allow five extra minutes because the lift near Platform 6 is temporarily unavailable. Staff will be at both platforms to provide directions. We apologise for the late notification and remind passengers to keep their tickets ready.\n\nPassengers changing from the 5:25 local service should remain on the footbridge and follow the blue West Bay signs. The 5:40 train will wait for that connection for up to three minutes, but it cannot be held beyond 5:43 because another service uses Platform 7. Anyone who misses the train may use the same ticket on the 6:10 departure. Bicycle spaces on the 6:10 are already full, so passengers travelling with bicycles should speak to station staff before leaving Platform 7. Further changes will appear in the transit app under “West Bay service”, not in general promotional notifications.",
    "grammarNote": "• 先判斷問題功能：purpose、what changed、what stayed、why、next。原句 instead of 常把舊資訊放成干擾。\n• 常錯：聽到 Platform 5 就選 5。辨認：What changed?—will depart from 7 instead of 5。無提示：用一句話回答下一步。遷移：把房間更換公告整理成「舊／新／不變／行動」。",
