    "goal": "although/even though + S+V；despite/in spite of + N/V-ing；however 連兩完整句並注意標點。",
    "article": "The city library planned to reopen its second floor on Monday. Although the renovation work was almost complete, the new lift had not passed its final inspection. The reading rooms could open; however, visitors who needed step-free access would not be able to reach them. Despite the delay, the library did not cancel all second-floor services.\n\nInstead, staff moved the most popular books and two computer stations to the ground floor. On the one hand, this reduced the amount of space near the entrance. On the other hand, it allowed more visitors to use the service safely. The library also extended the return date for items kept upstairs, so customers would not receive a late fee for books they could not collect.\n\nThe lift inspection was completed on Thursday, and normal access resumed on Friday. This final sentence belongs after the temporary arrangements because it closes the time line. If it appeared before the explanation of the ground-floor service, readers might think those arrangements were still needed after Friday. Connecting words do more than fill a blank: they show whether the next idea is a contrast, a result, an alternative, or the end of a temporary situation.\n\nFor the same reason, however cannot simply replace every connector. It signals a contrast, whereas therefore signals a result. Choosing between them requires understanding the relationship between two complete ideas, not memorising which word sounds more formal.",
    "listening": "The outdoor exhibition will open tomorrow as planned. However, the west entrance will remain closed because the path is being repaired. Although signs will direct visitors to the east entrance, the walk from the station will take about five minutes longer. Despite this inconvenience, all guided tours will begin at their original times. Visitors using wheelchairs may call the information desk for an alternative route. The repair is expected to finish on Wednesday; therefore, normal access should resume on Thursday. Please check the website before travelling in case the schedule changes.\n\nThe east entrance opens at nine thirty, whereas the first tour begins at ten. Visitors with a ten o'clock booking should arrive at least fifteen minutes early for ticket checks. On the other hand, people attending only the outdoor exhibition do not need a timed ticket. In spite of the longer route, the café and luggage desk will operate normally. If heavy rain delays the repair, Thursday's access update will be posted by six o'clock on Wednesday evening. Existing tour bookings will remain valid even if the west entrance is still unavailable.",
    "grammarNote": "• although/even though + S+V；despite/in spite of + N/V-ing；however 連兩完整句並注意標點。\n• 常錯：despite of、Although..., but...。辨認：___ being small, the room is useful. A Although B Despite。無提示：用 however 合併兩句。遷移：為維修公告寫問題、替代、恢復三句。",
