    "goal": "先行詞可隔著插入資訊；非限定 which 補充整個名詞。The shop, which opened in 2024, ...",
    "article": "Harbor Drinks, a small Taiwanese beverage company, opened its first overseas shop in 2024. Its main product is bubble tea, a drink that combines tea, milk or fruit flavour, and chewy tapioca balls. The company expected customers to recognise the bubbles, but a local consumer survey showed that many people did not know how to order the drink or choose a sweetness level.\n\nInstead of changing the product completely, Harbor Drinks changed the way it explained the menu. Each item now has a short description, and a simple table shows cup size, sweetness, ice level, and available toppings. New customers can choose a standard recipe, while experienced customers can customise their drink. Staff also offer small samples of the chewy topping because its texture is unfamiliar to some visitors.\n\nSales were slow during the first month. However, a video showing how each drink was prepared helped the product take off. Within six months, the shop had attracted both Taiwanese residents who missed a familiar flavour and local teenagers who enjoyed trying new combinations. The manager concluded that the product's overseas success did not come from removing its original character. It came from making an unfamiliar choice easier to understand. The same drink remained at the centre, but the service around it adapted to a new market.\n\nThe next survey will compare first-time and returning customers, so the company can see whether clear instructions lead people to try the drink again, not merely place one curious first order.",
    "listening": "Welcome to Harbor Drinks. If this is your first visit, start by selecting a tea base from the left side of the menu. Next, choose one of three sweetness levels. The regular recipe is marked with a blue circle, so you can order it without making any changes. Tapioca balls are included in our classic milk tea, but other toppings cost fifty cents. Customers who have food allergies should ask a staff member to check the ingredient list. During today's opening event, small samples are available near the entrance. After ordering, keep your number and collect your drink at the counter on the right.\n\nIf you are unsure about the chewy texture, try a sample before paying; a completed drink cannot be returned simply because you dislike a topping. Fruit teas can be prepared without milk, but the brown-sugar topping contains dairy. Wait times are currently about twelve minutes. Orders numbered 40 to 55 should remain near the collection counter, while later customers may sit upstairs. At four o'clock, staff will demonstrate how tapioca balls are prepared. The demonstration is free, although space is limited to twenty people. Add your name to the list beside the entrance if you wish to attend.",
    "grammarNote": "• 先行詞可隔著插入資訊；非限定 which 補充整個名詞。The shop, which opened in 2024, ...\n• 常錯：看到最近名詞就判指涉。辨認：a video showing how each drink was prepared helped the product take off，the product 指飲品，不是影片。無提示：找出 who/that/which 所指。遷移：為菜單寫一個人、一個物、一個地點關係句。",
