    "grammar": "G21 關係子句簡化",
    "goal": "主動：customers who use the site → customers using the site；被動：products that are sold → products sold。",
    "article": "Document 1 — Website announcement\n\nNorth Market is adding independent local sellers to its shopping website. Products sold by these businesses will appear beside North Market's own items. Customers using the marketplace can compare prices, delivery dates, and seller ratings on one page. The company says the change will put customer choice at the heart of the service. Each seller will remain responsible for product information, while North Market will handle payment and provide support if an order does not arrive.\n\nDocument 2 — Internal quality message\n\nDuring a two-week trial, web traffic increased by eighteen percent, but the support team also received questions about who was responsible for refunds. Several product descriptions submitted by sellers were unclear, and one item was advertised as environmentally friendly without evidence. Before the full launch, the marketplace page will be revised. Seller names will be displayed more clearly, the refund policy will be placed beside the payment button, and environmental claims will require supporting documents. The project manager has a long-term vision for the marketplace, but she does not want rapid growth to damage the customer experience. She recommends that the revised page be tested with ten customers before more sellers are invited.\n\nDocument 3 — Test instruction\n\nEach tester will find one local product, identify the seller, locate the delivery date, and explain how a refund would be requested. A task counts as complete only when the tester can point to the relevant information without assistance. The team will record time and errors separately; fast navigation alone will not be treated as a successful customer experience.",
    "listening": "Manager: We've reviewed the trial data. Customers liked comparing several sellers, but some couldn't tell who would issue a refund.\nDesigner: I can place the seller's name above the price and add a link to the refund terms beside the Buy button.\nManager: Good. Products advertised as sustainable must also include evidence approved by quality control.\nDesigner: Should we launch the changes to everyone on Friday?\nManager: Not yet. Have the revised page tested by ten customers first. If they can identify the seller and refund process, we'll release it next week.\n\nDesigner: Should all ten testers use the same product page?\n\nManager: No. Give them products from at least three sellers. We need to know whether the structure is clear across the marketplace, not only on the page we have reviewed most often.\n\nDesigner: I'll record how long they take and where they click. What counts as a successful task?\n\nManager: They must identify the seller, delivery date, and refund route without help. A fast result is not successful if they choose the wrong seller.\n\nDesigner: Understood. I'll run five tests on Wednesday and five on Thursday, then send a short evidence table by Friday morning.\n\nManager: Good. If one label repeatedly causes mistakes, revise it before inviting more sellers. Do not average away a problem that affects only one part of the process.",
