    "goal": "建立證據鏈：公告「每十分鐘」＋意見「charging interruption」＋結論「reliable」；選項若只說 electric＝successful，證據不足。",
    "article": "City notice — Green Loop transport trial\n\nFrom September, Green Loop will provide electric three-wheel shuttles between Central Station and Riverside Market. The existing bus comes only every forty minutes and does not stop directly outside the market. The new vehicles are intended to fill this gap. They will run every ten minutes from 8:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m., and a single trip will cost NT$30. The vehicles produce no exhaust fumes beside the road, although the electricity used for charging will still be included in the overall energy review.\n\nPassenger feedback — Week one\n\nMost interviewed passengers found the service convenient, especially when carrying shopping bags. Affordability was another attraction: a taxi on the same route costs about NT$120 on average. However, some passengers could not find the Central Station boarding point, and two evening trips were interrupted because a battery needed charging.\n\nThe city has therefore taken three measures. It has placed route maps at station exits, added a spare battery, and put up money for better charging equipment beside the market. Drivers will also report every missed trip instead of recording only the number of successful journeys.\n\nEight-week review plan\n\nThe trial will continue for eight weeks. A lot depends on whether the service remains reliable during busy periods, not simply on whether electric vehicles sound environmentally friendly. At the end, officials will compare passenger numbers, missed trips, energy use, and customer feedback. They will also check whether the service appeals to older passengers and people carrying goods, rather than only to tourists trying it once.\n\nIf the evidence shows that the shuttle is both affordable and reliable, the route may become permanent. If charging continues to cancel trips, the city may change the timetable or add another vehicle before making that decision. The environmental label alone will not determine the result.",
    "listening": "Attention, Green Loop passengers. Because one vehicle is being charged, the 6:20 service from Riverside Market will not operate. The 6:30 and 6:40 trips are expected to run normally. Passengers who cannot wait may use Bus 18 from the main road; Green Loop tickets will be accepted on that bus this evening. Staff are placing temporary signs between the market entrance and the bus stop. We apologise for the disruption. Please check the route table in the app for real-time updates before choosing your next trip.\n\nBus 18 leaves from Stop C, which is approximately four minutes from the market entrance. It does not stop at Central Station's south door; passengers should get off at North Street and walk across the covered bridge. Anyone requiring step-free access may wait for the 6:30 Green Loop trip or ask staff to arrange an accessible taxi at no extra charge. The city will record how many passengers use each alternative and whether the charged vehicle returns for the 7:00 service. A further announcement will be made at 6:45. If you transfer to Bus 18, keep the Green Loop ticket until the end of your journey because the driver must scan it.",
    "grammarNote": "• 建立證據鏈：公告「每十分鐘」＋意見「charging interruption」＋結論「reliable」；選項若只說 electric＝successful，證據不足。\n• 常錯：把 expected 改成 guaranteed；把 may 改成 will。辨認：may become permanent 的強度。無提示：指出一個明示事實與一步推論。遷移：依表格與公告選替代班次。",
