    "goal": "must/should be + p.p.、will be + p.p.；製造公告以物為主詞常用被動。",
    "article": "Three engineering graduates identified a market gap: small food businesses needed affordable temperature sensors, but most systems were designed for large factories. The group formed a start-up to produce a simpler device. Their first challenge was funding. A bank would not provide a large loan because the company had no sales history, so the founders launched a crowdfunding campaign. Hundreds of supporters contributed small amounts, and enough money was raised to build fifty devices.\n\nBefore production began, a safety procedure was written and every machine was inspected. The first assembly line could produce ten units a day, but output was not increased immediately. Each device had to be tested at three temperatures, and any defect had to be recorded. During the first week, four sensors failed the test because a wire had been placed too close to a hot part. The design was revised before the next batch was produced.\n\nThe founders wanted to be their own bosses, but they learned that running a business also requires collective effort. Suppliers, technicians, customers, and the people who supported the campaign all influenced the result. Crowdfunding solved the first money problem; it did not remove the need for quality control. The company could grow only if the device remained safe, useful, and affordable for the market it was created to serve.\n\nBefore accepting a second round of funding, the founders will publish the failure rate, explain the design change, and confirm that the next fifty devices pass the same three-temperature test.",
    "listening": "Production supervisor: Before today's shift, all machines must be inspected and the emergency stop buttons must be tested. We plan to produce forty units, but speed is not the only target. After assembly, each unit will be checked for loose wires and operated for thirty minutes. Defective items should be placed in the red area and must not be sent to packaging. If more than three units fail, notify me immediately; the line will be stopped for a process review. The output report is due by five, and it should include both the number produced and the number that passed inspection.\n\nThe first ten units will also be tested at low temperature because last week's failures appeared only after cooling. Use the revised checklist dated 14 May; the earlier version does not include that step. If a wire is too close to the heated panel, photograph its position before moving the unit to the red area. Do not repair it on the active line. At two o'clock, the engineer will review the photographs and decide whether production can continue. Packaging staff should prepare boxes but must wait for the inspection release. A high output total will not meet today's target unless the safety checks are complete and the passing number is recorded separately.",
    "grammarNote": "• must/should be + p.p.、will be + p.p.；製造公告以物為主詞常用被動。\n• 常錯：must inspected。辨認：Every item must ___. A test B be tested。無提示：The line will ___ if four fail. 遷移：把三項 SOP 寫成被動公告。",
