    "title": "睡眠、記憶與工作表現",
    "stage": "TOEIC 應用",
    "grammar": "G19 名詞子句遷移",
    "goal": "Research suggests that + 完整子句；check whether + 完整子句；what + 不完整子句。",
    "article": "A service centre introduced late training sessions because daytime calls were increasing. Employees attended a two-hour class after their shifts and returned early the next morning. Although the course material was clear, quiz results fell during the second week. Some managers first assumed that the employees needed more practice. However, a short survey indicated that many were sleeping less than six hours.\n\nThe training team changed the schedule. Half of the material was moved to a self-paced morning activity, and evening sessions ended an hour earlier. Employees were also asked to complete a short recall task the next day rather than repeat the lesson immediately. The aim was to give their brains time to take in and organise new information. After three weeks, the group remembered more and reported less fatigue.\n\nThe result does not prove that one schedule will work for everyone. It does show why sleep should be considered when learning performance changes. Too little sleep can reduce concentration, and that problem may have a knock-on effect: a worker misses one instruction, enters incorrect data, and then needs extra time to fix the record. When a decision is complex but not urgent, it may also be useful to sleep on it—to wait until the next day after thinking. This expression does not mean avoiding the decision. It means allowing time for careful processing before choosing.",
    "listening": "Trainer: Before tomorrow's assessment, don't spend the whole night reading the manual. Review the three action steps, then stop at your normal bedtime. The assessment checks whether you can apply the process, not whether you can repeat every sentence. When you arrive, you will first read a customer message, identify the problem, and choose a next action. After that, you will explain your evidence to a partner. If you are unsure about one item, mark it and continue; do not let one question use all your time. The results will be reviewed with you individually on Friday, and any weak skill will be practised in a new situation.\n\nPlease arrive by eight forty-five. The first case begins at nine, and late arrivals will not receive extra time. You may bring water, but phones and printed notes must remain in your locker. The assessment has two sections of twenty minutes with a five-minute break between them. During the break, do not discuss answers, because your partner may receive the cases in a different order. If you finish early, check that every action is supported by a detail in the customer message. A familiar phrase is not enough by itself. On Friday, your review will compare the evidence you selected, the time used, and the reason for each error; it will not give a medical conclusion about tiredness.",
    "grammarNote": "• Research suggests that + 完整子句；check whether + 完整子句；what + 不完整子句。\n• 常錯：what/that 只憑中文「什麼／那個」選。辨認：The test checks ___ you can apply it. A whether B what you can apply it。無提示：Explain ___ caused the error. 遷移：寫一個研究結論與限制。",
