    "id": "U30",
    "number": 30,
    "title": "廣告如何影響購買決定",
    "stage": "TOEIC 應用",
    "grammar": "G25 比較指標與避免過度推論",
    "goal": "讀比較文先標「指標、時間範圍、方向」。B：same-day orders↑；A：month returns↓。不可改成 B overall better。",
    "article": "An online electronics store tested two advertisements for the same headphones. Advertisement A listed battery life, warranty length, price, and customer-service hours. Advertisement B used a popular athlete's endorsement and a message saying, Thousands have already chosen this model—offer ends tonight. Both ads led to sales, but they encouraged different ways of deciding.\n\nAdvertisement A asked customers to compare product evidence. Advertisement B offered two mental shortcuts. The athlete's endorsement invited people to transfer their trust in the athlete to the product. The phrase about thousands of buyers provided social proof: if many people had chosen it, the model appeared safer. The deadline also encouraged an impulse purchase by reducing the time available for comparison.\n\nThe store's report showed that Advertisement B produced more same-day orders, while Advertisement A led to fewer returns during the following month. This does not necessarily mean that factual ads are always better or that endorsements are dishonest. The two results measure different things. One shows immediate sales; the other suggests whether buyers understood the product well enough to keep it.\n\nBefore approving the next campaign, the marketing manager requested that both advertisements include the same warranty and return information. She also asked the team to measure not only clicks and orders but also cancellations, returns, and customer questions. A persuasive campaign may increase revenue, but a complete review must examine what happens after the purchase as well.",
    "listening": "Marketing lead: The new campaign received many clicks, but completed orders increased only slightly.\nAnalyst: The advertisement sends users to the product page, yet the total price appears only after a service charge is added at checkout.\nLead: That may explain why people leave. We should display the full price earlier.\nAnalyst: I agree. I also suggest that we test the phrase Only three left. Stock changes quickly, so the message may become inaccurate.\nLead: Good point. Please prepare a revised version with the full price and a live stock number. We'll compare completed orders and complaints for one week before choosing the final ad.\n\nAnalyst: Should we keep the athlete's endorsement in both versions?\n\nLead: Yes. If we remove it from one version, we won't know whether the result came from price display or from the familiar face. Keep the image, product description, and target audience the same.\n\nAnalyst: What about the countdown clock?\n\nLead: Remove it unless the offer truly ends at that time. We should not create urgency with inaccurate information.\n\nAnalyst: I'll set up two pages. Page A will show the service charge beside the advertised price. Page B will show the same total only at checkout.\n\nLead: Good. Record completed orders, cancellations within twenty-four hours, and customer questions. A higher click rate alone will not be enough to choose the campaign.\n\nAnalyst: I'll send the test plan for approval before the pages go live on Monday.",
    "grammarNote": "• 讀比較文先標「指標、時間範圍、方向」。B：same-day orders↑；A：month returns↓。不可改成 B overall better。\n• 常錯：把 correlation 當完整原因，把 may explain 當 proved。辨認強度；無提示：寫出一個保守結論。遷移：比較兩版 HMI 的點擊、完成率、錯誤率。",
