    "goal": "實際意思：錯題不是只記答案，先分「沒定位、強度誤讀、範圍偷換、搭配不熟、時間線錯」。",
    "article": "Project brief and revision note\n\nBrief — Visitor welcome video\n\nThe museum needs a ninety-second video for first-time visitors. It must show the entrance from the railway station, the location of the ticket machines, and the rule that large bags should be left at the storage desk. The tone should be friendly and calm. Please include English captions and leave five seconds at the end for the booking address. Do not show exhibitions that will close before the video is published. The first version is due on 12 August; publication is planned for 20 August.\n\nReview of Version 1\n\nThe production company delivered a visually attractive two-minute film. It opened with a fast tour of the museum's most colourful rooms and used energetic music. The final image included the booking address. In an informal creative sense, the film looked polished, but it had not fully understood the assignment. It did not show the route from the station or the storage desk, and it featured a temporary exhibition ending on 15 August. English captions were included, but several disappeared too quickly to read.\n\nThe team therefore asked the company to get three sections redone. The request did not mean starting the entire project again. The entrance footage could stay, and the music licence was still valid. The editor needed to shorten the exhibition sequence, replace the closing exhibit with the bag-storage procedure, and slow the captions. A new station-to-entrance clip also had to be recorded.\n\nVersion 2 outcome\n\nThe revised video lasted eighty-eight seconds and met the brief. It showed every required location and left six seconds for the booking address. Test viewers could read all captions. One reviewer wrote that the editor had “understood the assignment”: the video not only satisfied each clear requirement but also made an unfamiliar visit feel manageable. Another reviewer said it exceeded expectations because it used a split-screen map without adding extra length.\n\nThis case shows why a beautiful result may still miss the mark. Quality must be judged against the requested purpose, audience, content, and deadline—not against appearance alone.",
    "listening": "Manager: I reviewed the draft visitor video. The images are excellent, but we need to check them against the brief before approving it.\n\nEditor: I know it's twelve seconds too long. I can shorten the opening.\n\nManager: Please do, but length is not the only issue. The station clip ends before the sign for the museum appears. A first-time visitor may not know which exit to use.\n\nEditor: I have another shot that includes Exit Four and the pedestrian crossing. It is less dramatic, but it is clearer.\n\nManager: Use that one. Also, the caption says that bags “can” be left at storage. The visitor rule says bags larger than forty centimetres “must” be left there. We should not weaken a requirement.\n\nEditor: Understood. I'll change the modal and keep the measurement on screen for four seconds. Do we need to replace the background music?\n\nManager: No. The music meets the brief, and the licence covers online use. Keep it. Please send the revised cut by three tomorrow afternoon so that the accessibility team has time to check the captions.\n\nEditor: I'll deliver it by two. I'll include a change list showing the new route clip, the corrected rule, and the final length.\n\nManager: Good. If those points are complete, we can approve the film without another full meeting.",
    "grammarNote": "• 實際意思：錯題不是只記答案，先分「沒定位、強度誤讀、範圍偷換、搭配不熟、時間線錯」。\n• 原句：Version 1 的錯不是一般品質差，而是未符合 brief 的指定內容。\n• 結構：需求（must/should/do not）→ 成品證據 → 缺口 → 最小修正。\n• 常見錯誤：把 three sections 擴成 entire project；把 included captions 當 readable captions；把 attractive 當 meet brief。\n• 辨認：must 是硬性要求。無提示：列 Version 1 三個缺口。遷移：拿活動需求表逐項審核海報，僅修改不合格處。",
