    "goal": "實際意思：比較兩次可信模考或兩輪練習，要看相同 Part 的正確數、耗時、錯因，而非只看總感覺。",
    "article": "Hybrid-work pilot: policy, results, and staff response\n\nNorthline Support tested hybrid working for twelve weeks. Sixty service employees split their time between home and the main office: two fixed office days for team training and three location-flexible days. Managers stopped using online status as the main measure of productivity. Instead, the pilot tracked completed cases, correction rates, response time, and customer satisfaction.\n\nThe big upside for employees was control over commuting time. In a survey, 47 of 60 participants valued the arrangement at more than a small monthly pay increase. Average completed cases rose by 6 per cent, and customer satisfaction remained stable. However, the figures were not equally positive for every task. New staff needed longer to sort out unusual cases on home days, while experienced staff handled routine work slightly faster away from the office.\n\nThe training team therefore proposed a change rather than a complete return to the old system. During each new employee's first six weeks, one flexible day would become an additional office day. The purpose was to provide face-to-face contact for difficult decisions, not to monitor every minute. After six weeks, the employee could move to the standard schedule if accuracy reached the agreed level.\n\nSome remote employees raised a separate concern. They felt that ideas mentioned in office conversations reached managers sooner than suggestions sent through the project board. This possible proximity bias could affect who received interesting assignments. Northline responded by requiring every project proposal and decision to be recorded in the shared system, even when it began in a face-to-face conversation.\n\nThe pilot does not show that hybrid work is best for every organisation. Northline already had secure systems, measurable service tasks, and staff who could work remotely. A factory, laboratory, or front desk may have different needs. The evidence supports a narrower conclusion: for this team, an output-based policy maintained service quality and offered flexibility, provided that new staff received extra support and informal decisions were made visible.\n\nFollow-up email: The revised pilot begins 1 September. Team leads must publish office training days by 20 August. Employees do not need to choose their flexible locations until the preceding Friday.",
    "listening": "Team lead: Before the revised hybrid schedule starts, I want to explain how performance will be reviewed. We are not going to count the number of minutes that your status light is green.\n\nEmployee: What will you use instead?\n\nTeam lead: For routine support cases, we will look at completed cases, corrections, and customer response time. For project work, each team will agree on a deliverable and deadline at the beginning of the month. A difficult project cannot be compared with ten simple tickets by number alone.\n\nEmployee: If I need help on a home day, should I wait until we're in the office?\n\nTeam lead: No. Post the question in the shared case channel. If it involves customer safety or a service interruption, call the duty manager immediately. We want to sort out urgent problems when they occur.\n\nEmployee: I heard that new staff will have three office days. Is that permanent?\n\nTeam lead: Only for their first six weeks, unless a person and manager agree that more support is needed. The extra day is for guided practice, not punishment.\n\nEmployee: How will you make sure remote people hear about new projects?\n\nTeam lead: Every opportunity will be posted on the project board for at least two working days. A manager may discuss an idea in the office, but no assignment will be final until everyone can see the description and express interest.\n\nEmployee: That sounds fair. I'll check that my notification settings are on before September.",
    "grammarNote": "• 實際意思：比較兩次可信模考或兩輪練習，要看相同 Part 的正確數、耗時、錯因，而非只看總感覺。\n• 原句概念：productivity 需多指標；同理 test performance 需正確率＋時間＋猜題原因。\n• 結構：baseline → same measure → change → limitation／next adjustment。\n• 常錯：題目難度不同仍直接比總分；一次波動當穩定提升；用做題分鐘數代替有效產出。\n• 辨認：哪個指標不能單用？online time。無提示：寫出自己兩次 Part 7 可比的三項。遷移：若正確數相同但未完成題減少，記為節奏改善，不捏造換算分數。",
