    "goal": "實際意思：後段錯多可能是內容、時間壓力或疲勞；需要對照，不先貼標籤。",
    "article": "Wellness programme review: energy across a long service day\n\nA travel-service centre wanted to reduce late-afternoon errors during its busiest month. Instead of promising one secret for perfect concentration, it tested a group of small habits with eighty volunteers. Half worked their usual schedule. The other half joined a six-week programme: a brief morning planning session, water available at every desk, a communal meal twice a week, and two ten-minute walking breaks. No employee was asked to follow a special diet, although the lunch menu added more vegetables, beans, fish, and whole grains similar to foods common in a Mediterranean diet.\n\nAt the end of six weeks, the programme group made 12 per cent fewer address-entry errors between three and five in the afternoon. Their morning error rate changed very little. They also reported feeling more socially connected, especially employees who lived alone rather than in a multigenerational household. The usual-schedule group showed no clear change.\n\nThe result is useful but incomplete. Employees chose whether to volunteer, so the programme group may have started with a more positive attitude toward health. Four changes were introduced together; the review cannot show whether water, walking, food, or communal contact caused the difference. The company also did not measure whether the effect continued after the programme ended.\n\nFor the next stage, both groups will keep the same lunch menu, but only one group will receive scheduled walking reminders. This narrower comparison may provide better evidence about the breaks. The company will also check performance eight weeks later. It will not describe the programme as a method that makes everyone age well or remain young at heart. Its practical question is smaller: can sustainable daily habits help employees maintain accurate work during a long shift?\n\nThe training manager connected the finding to test endurance. A learner may perform well on the first thirty questions but lose accuracy later. The response should not be “try harder” without evidence. Record where accuracy falls, then test one change—break timing during practice, hydration, sleep routine, or pacing—while keeping other conditions as stable as possible. Health advice should remain general; persistent fatigue or medical concerns require qualified professional guidance.",
    "listening": "Trainer: I compared your two ninety-minute practice sessions. In both, your accuracy was about eighty per cent during the first hour. In the final thirty minutes, it fell to sixty-two per cent on Saturday and sixty-four per cent on Wednesday.\n\nLearner: So the problem is probably vocabulary near the end.\n\nTrainer: Possibly, but the missed questions came from several topics. The common feature was timing: you spent too long on one triple passage, then answered the last twelve questions in seven minutes.\n\nLearner: Should I take a long break in the middle?\n\nTrainer: Not during a real TOEIC test. During training, however, we can separate knowledge from endurance. Tomorrow, do the final thirty minutes as a fresh set. If accuracy returns to your earlier level, fatigue or pacing is more likely than a sudden vocabulary gap.\n\nLearner: And if it remains low?\n\nTrainer: Then analyse the question types and language. For the next full practice, set a checkpoint before the triple passages and move on when one question is using too much time. Keep sleep, start time, and materials similar so that the comparison is meaningful.\n\nLearner: Should I change my food and study schedule at the same time?\n\nTrainer: Change one factor first. We need evidence about what helps you. Also, if unusual fatigue continues outside study, ask a qualified health professional rather than treating test data as a medical diagnosis.",
    "grammarNote": "• 實際意思：後段錯多可能是內容、時間壓力或疲勞；需要對照，不先貼標籤。\n• 原句：fresh final set 若恢復，較支持 endurance/pacing；若仍低，再看題型與語言。\n• 結構：觀察位置 → 提出多個解釋 → 控制條件測一項 → 記結果。\n• 常錯：一次後段失誤就判定單字差；練習同時改睡眠、策略、題本，無法比較。\n• 辨認：哪項應固定？start time/materials。無提示：寫一個可測假設。遷移：Part 3 後半錯多，隔日以新材料做等長後半組，仍一次一題解析錯因。",
