    "goal": "實際意思：第三次可信模考或第三輪資料要看「同類錯因是否連續改善」，不是只看單次高低。",
    "article": "Compressed-week trial: three documents\n\nDocument 1 — Trial notice\n\nBrightPath Design will test a compressed working week from September through November. Full-time employees will work the same thirty-six weekly hours over four longer days instead of five standard days. Each department must keep customer support available Monday to Friday, so teams will use different days off. Salaries and annual leave will not change. The trial is not a reduction in total contracted hours.\n\nDocument 2 — Interim results after six weeks\n\nOverall project output remained within 2 per cent of the previous quarter, and the proportion of deadlines met rose from 91 to 94 per cent. Sick-day use fell slightly. However, the average hides a departmental difference. The research team, whose work can often be arranged around long independent blocks, completed reports faster. The client-support team handled the same number of cases but recorded 18 per cent more corrections during the final hour of its longer days.\n\nSeveral employees valued the extra day away from work and reported a better work-life balance. Others said that caring responsibilities were harder to arrange around a ten-hour day. Two freelance designers also noted that a four-day schedule was different for them: freelance work can offer freedom, and sometimes a lucrative career, but a nominal day off has little meaning when a client deadline requires weekend work.\n\nDocument 3 — Management response\n\nThe company will continue the trial, but the support department may finish after nine hours and complete the remaining time in a short Friday shift. Management will compare correction rates again in October. It will also ask whether people actually used the free day for rest or simply moved unpaid tasks to it.\n\nThe early result does not prove that a compressed week always improves performance. Output was maintained overall, yet one team showed a late-day accuracy problem. The important question is not only whether fewer workdays look attractive, but at what cost the schedule is achieved. If work is pushed into longer, tiring days or hidden weekend hours, the label “four-day week” may describe the calendar without describing the real workload.\n\nUpdate: October corrections in client support returned close to the earlier level after the nine-hour limit. Management will keep collecting data through November before making a permanent decision.",
    "listening": "Operations director: We now have October data from the compressed-week trial. Project output is still stable, but I want to discuss the support team's correction rate.\n\nSupport manager: After we limited the long days to nine hours, corrections in the final hour fell from eighteen per cent above baseline to three per cent above it. That is close to the variation we normally see from month to month.\n\nDirector: Did the short Friday shift create a service gap?\n\nManager: No. Half the team works early Friday and half late Friday. Customer response time remained under our four-hour target. However, scheduling is more complex, and supervisors spend about one extra hour each week arranging coverage.\n\nEmployee representative: Staff feedback is mixed. Most people prefer the new pattern, but parents who collect young children find the longer days difficult. Could they keep five shorter days if their role is covered?\n\nDirector: The trial was designed to test an option, not force one schedule on everyone. Please propose criteria for choosing the five-day pattern. The criteria must be based on service coverage and employee circumstances, not on whether a manager personally prefers to see someone every day.\n\nManager: I'll prepare the criteria and the November rota by next Wednesday.\n\nDirector: Good. In the final report, show the improvement in corrections, the stable response time, and the extra scheduling work. We need the benefits and the cost before deciding.",
    "grammarNote": "• 實際意思：第三次可信模考或第三輪資料要看「同類錯因是否連續改善」，不是只看單次高低。\n• 原句概念：18%→3% 且服務時間穩定，支持修改有效的可能；仍要納入排班成本與更多月份。\n• 結構：baseline → intervention → repeated result → variation／cost → provisional decision。\n• 常錯：總體持平就忽略子群；percent above baseline 當成正確率；一次回落就說永久解決。\n• 辨認：哪個成本新增？排班時間。無提示：用保守語氣寫結果。遷移：三次 Part 3 的否定題錯誤 6→3→3，可說改善後暫穩，不換算分數。",
